<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hudson Valley</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hudson Valley is the valley of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-river">Hudson River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, running north from New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a> City towards Albany. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> settled it as the core of New Netherland, granting large patroonships such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rensselaerswyck">Rensselaerswyck</a>. Under English rule great manor estates dominated it, and Dutch language, place names and customs persisted there long after 1664.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hudson-valley.jpg" alt="Hudson Valley" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UpstateNYer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BrunswickAutumn.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
